<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assassination of Julius Caesar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> was the killing of the Roman dictator by a group of senators in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 44 BCE. The conspirators aimed to restore the Republic, but his death led instead to further civil wars. These wars ended with the victory of Caesar's heir Octavian, who became Augustus and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assassination-of-julius-caesar.jpg" alt="Assassination of Julius Caesar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vincenzo Camuccini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vincenzo_Camuccini_-_La_morte_di_Cesare_(cropped_3-2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
